; selftest-leavelevel.eval - handed to the runner by `Eval.ps1 -SelfTest`, FIRST
; in a batch with resettest.eval; must PASS, and must leave the party OFF the
; harness level for the reset that follows it.
;
; THE RESET HAD NO LEVEL TO COME BACK FROM (code-review C300). `reset` re-read
; whatever level the party stood on, so a suite batched after this one ran on
; whatever this one left - and an ambush leaves "~encounter", which has no file:
; the re-read hit the map loader's assert and the run died on a CRT dialog. It
; now goes back to the harness level by a real load, and resettest.eval's blocks
; after it must match its solo run's line for line.
;
; Every way off the level the harness has, in one walk: `goto` (a real level
; change, which STASHES the level left behind), out of that dungeon onto the
; world map (which PARKS the one walked out of), and an ambush on the road (which
; REPLACES the level under the world map with a generated one). Then out of the
; ambush too, so the current level is "~encounter" and the party is on the world
; map - the exact shape the issue reproduced. The reset must forget all of it:
; the stash, the parked level, the encounter.
;
; THE HARNESS LEVEL IS CARVED BEFORE IT IS LEFT, so its stash is NOT its file. A
; level load takes a stash over the file, and the switch back is a level load:
; if the reset kept the stashes, resettest.eval's first baseline would come up
; in this arena (its `mapinfo` line differs) instead of the authored level. Left
; uncarved, the stash equals the file and that leak would read as identical.
; The `stashed` line of the last `transients` below names every level held, and
; the self-test demands the harness level among them - something to forget.
;
; AND AN UNDO STEP IN CRYPT1 (code-review C297). The ambush puts a generated
; level where crypt1 was, and every undo step is a snapshot of crypt1 - an undo
; inside the encounter used to restore crypt1's map under "~encounter". Walking
; out onto the world map keeps the history (crypt1 is parked, not replaced), so
; the ambush is what must drop it. A readout on EACH SIDE of the ambush, so the
; verdict is that one transition's and no other's: on crypt1 the step is
; counted (the paint took one), on the world map it still is (the walk out kept
; it - "transients on crypt1" again, since the parked level is still current),
; and inside the encounter, before its own `leave`, there is none. Read across
; all three transitions instead, a walk out or an encounter's leave that began
; clearing the history would hide an ambush that stopped. Two paints of one
; square, so at least one is an edit; never saved, and the reset after this
; script forgets crypt1's stash.
logecho on
reset
seed 3
arena open 9 9
goto crypt1
editor place floors floor_slabs 5 7
editor place floors floor_temple 5 7
mappage close
transients
leave
worldpos 6 6
transients
encounter
transients
leave
state
; The level this leaves behind, named - the self-test reads this line to know
; the batch really did start resettest.eval somewhere else, and its `stashed`
; line to know there was something for the reset to forget.
transients
